<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle trade at standstill - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle trade at standstill - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading was at a standstill early Friday, USDA said. Buyer inquiry was good and most seeking additional live inventory. Seller interest nil. Weekly volume 77,900.  Live basis sales - Equivalent 3 percent shrink delivered and FOB, some FOB 4% shrink. Dressed basis delivered (paid on hot carcass weights)</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers -  No reported sales.</p>
<p>Slaughter Heifers - No reported sales.</p>
<p>Sales confirmed - None    For the week -</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
